"""
consciousness.py — Global Workspace, Memory Replay & Reasoning Module

Core mechanisms based on neuroscientific theory:

1. GLOBAL WORKSPACE THEORY (Baars 1988 / Dehaene 2011)
   When ≥ IGNITION_REGIONS brain regions exhibit simultaneous activity
   above IGNITION_THRESHOLD, a 'global broadcast' fires — sending a
   reactivation pulse to every region.  This models conscious attention:
   the winning neural coalition becomes "globally available".

2. HIPPOCAMPAL MEMORY REPLAY (Replay/Consolidation)
   During quiet periods (low total activity) the hippocampus replays its
   hottest engrams (neurons that fired most recently/frequently) back into
   the association cortex, strengthening stored patterns — like dreaming
   or offline consolidation.

3. AUTONOMOUS REASONING (Association-chain inference)
   The module tracks recent semantic concepts (from web + speech inputs)
   and periodically detects pairs with overlapping activation sequences.
   Detected connections are injected back as text into the brain's
   semantic pathway, driving further exploration — emergent curiosity.

4. INNER MONOLOGUE (Stream of Consciousness)
   Every MONOLOGUE_INTERVAL ticks a one-sentence self-description is
   generated combining: dominant emotion + current goal + active concept
   + motor output.  Exported as brain.consciousness_stream (deque).

Data classes are grouped into sections:
  1a. SensorChannel / SensorHealthBoard — per-sensor availability tracking
  1b. SelfModel                         — persistent first-person identity
  2.  EpisodicMemory                    — tick-stamped autobiography
  3+. All remaining subsystems (20+ classes)
"""

